5,1,1,talk,Shion,,"Since we can't keep using the room for everything, we should be logical. I'll look into the partition wall to the office and crumbs and bins at the desks.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Daisuke,,I... I think we should be careful about the costs. I'll check the invoices for outside hire by the hour and the quotes for the two fit-outs.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Rin,,I want to know who actually uses the room! I'll check the fortnight's tally of use by person and the final clear-out of the old fridge.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Servas,,It is important to consider the human element of our workspace. I shall look into the unplanned talk since the refit and where the last awkward conversation happened.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Toshio,,I will look into the facilities callouts on this floor and the round trip for a hot lunch.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Shion,,"Does anyone else feel that the current lack of a clear rule is the main problem, or are we focusing too much on the physical space?","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I think both matter... but if we don't know the budget, we might pick something we can't actually afford.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Rin,,"But the budget isn't the only thing! If we just pick something expensive that nobody likes, it's a waste of money anyway, right?","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Servas,,Rin makes a fair point. A room is more than its price tag; it is the heart of how we interact. We must ensure it serves our spirits as well as our needs.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Toshio,,"Efficiency is the only way to ensure the room doesn't become a burden. If the upkeep is too high, the spirit of the room will suffer regardless of its purpose.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, efficiency is fine, but if the room is just ""efficient"" and doesn't solve the noise and mess issues, it's still a failure. We need a purpose that actually fits the environment.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Daisuke,,I agree with Shion... I just don't want us to make a decision and then find out later that we can't actually pay for it.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Rin,,"I just want it to be fair! If we find out that only a few people are using it, maybe we should change how we share it.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Servas,,"Fairness is a noble goal, Rin. However, we must also ask if the room can provide a sanctuary for the difficult conversations that currently have no home.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, a sanctuary is useless if it requires constant maintenance that falls on one person. We need to see the data on how the space is actually managed before we dream of sanctuaries.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Shion,,"Let's just see what the data says first. I'm satisfied with my choices, so I'll pass for now.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
21,1,4,pass,Shion,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
22,1,4,talk,Daisuke,,I'll wait for the results too.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
