39,2,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
40,2,1,talk,Shion,,"It's clear that the room's current state is a nuisance. The walls are far too thin for privacy, and eating at our desks is creating a mess that needs daily attention.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"The outside hire costs are actually quite high, and the fit-out quotes show a significant difference in price between a kitchen and a meeting space.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,1,talk,Rin,,"It's not fair at all! Only two people are using the room almost all the time, and someone keeps having to clean up a fridge full of stuff that doesn't even belong to anyone!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It is disheartening to see that our connections have withered; we have no space for unplanned talk, and our most difficult moments are played out in front of everyone.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The time spent walking for lunch is excessive, and the lack of facilities callouts for the store room suggests that simplicity is the only way to avoid a maintenance burden.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Daisuke, since you saw the quotes, is the meeting space significantly more expensive than the kitchen? If the walls are this thin, a meeting room might just be a noise chamber.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,"It is... yes, the meeting space is more expensive. About 141,000 yen compared to 96,000 for the kitchen. But we are already spending a lot on outside rentals.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,2,talk,Rin,,"Wait, if we're spending so much on rentals, why not just make the room a place where everyone can actually use it, instead of just two people?","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,2,talk,Servas,,"If we prioritize only the numbers, we risk ignoring the loneliness of our office. We need a space that encourages us to speak and heal, not just a place to save yen.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Servas, healing is a luxury we cannot afford if we are wasting twenty-five minutes on a lunch trip. A kitchen would solve a practical inefficiency that affects everyone daily.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Toshio, a kitchen might solve the lunch trip, but it doesn't solve the privacy issue. If we can hear everything through the walls, a kitchen just adds smells to the noise.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I suppose that's true. But if we keep renting outside rooms for small groups, we're just paying for a problem we could solve here, even if it's expensive.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,3,talk,Rin,,"But if we make it a meeting room, will the two people who use it all the time just keep hogging it? We need a rule so everyone gets a turn!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,3,talk,Servas,,"A rule is a start, Rin, but a Quiet Room could offer the peace we lack. It would be a sanctuary for reflection and a place to step away from the noise of the office.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,3,talk,Toshio,,A Quiet Room doesn't address the lunch waste or the rental costs. We should prioritize a solution that removes a daily burden from everyone's schedule.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,2,4,talk,Shion,,"If we want to stop the mess at the desks, a kitchen is the most logical choice, provided we can actually manage the cleaning this time.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,2,4,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm still worried about the cost, but if it stops the daily rental payments, it might actually save us money in the long run.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,2,4,talk,Rin,,"I just don't want the same person to end up doing all the cleaning again! If we have a kitchen, we need a real plan for the fridge!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,2,4,talk,Servas,,"A kitchen may feed the body, but it does not feed the soul. We must consider if a space for quiet reflection or private conversation is more vital for our harmony.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,2,4,talk,Toshio,,"Harmony is a byproduct of a well-functioning environment. If we eliminate the daily stress of the lunch commute and the clutter at our desks, the harmony will follow naturally.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
