63,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
64,3,,status,Servas,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
65,3,1,talk,Shion,,"Given the evidence, a kitchen solves the desk mess and the lunch commute, but a meeting space addresses the rental costs and the lack of privacy. I'm leaning toward the kitchen.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"I'm torn, but the rental costs are a constant drain. However, the kitchen is cheaper to install and seems to help more people daily. I think I'll vote for the kitchen.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Rin,,"I'll vote for the kitchen too, but only if we make a strict rule about the fridge so it's fair for everyone!","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Servas,,I fear we are neglecting the need for a sanctuary. A Quiet Room would provide the peace and privacy we so desperately lack for our mental well-being.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Toshio,,The data is clear: the lunch commute is a waste of time and the desk clutter is an inefficiency. I vote for the Open Kitchen.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Servas, I respect your view, but a Quiet Room doesn't solve the practical problems we've identified. We need a functional solution first.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"I... I agree. While a sanctuary sounds nice, the financial drain of the rentals and the daily mess are more urgent problems to solve.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,2,talk,Rin,,"Yeah! Plus, if we have a kitchen, maybe we can all eat together and be less lonely, which helps Servas too!","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,2,talk,Servas,,"That is a heartwarming thought, Rin. Perhaps a shared meal is its own form of sanctuary, though I still worry about where we shall go when we need true silence.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"Silence can be found in the gaps between our tasks, but hunger and clutter are constant. The kitchen is the only choice that optimizes our time and space.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Shion,,"It seems we have a strong consensus. Unless anyone has a sudden change of heart, the kitchen is the most logical path forward for the office.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I'll stick with the kitchen. It's the most affordable fit-out and it addresses the most immediate issues we've discussed.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,3,talk,Rin,,"Kitchen it is! As long as we all help clean up, it'll be the best room ever!","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,3,talk,Servas,,"I shall yield to the majority. If a shared meal can bring us closer and ease the burdens of the day, then I will support the Open Kitchen.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,3,talk,Toshio,,I agree. The decision is based on practical data and collective benefit. I vote for the Open Kitchen.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Shion,,Then it is settled. I vote for the Open Kitchen.,"{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
81,3,4,talk,Daisuke,,I vote for the Open Kitchen.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
82,3,4,talk,Rin,,I vote for the Open Kitchen!,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
83,3,4,talk,Servas,,I vote for the Open Kitchen.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
84,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I vote for the Open Kitchen.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
